	explicit_bzero(), fls(), strlcpy() and strlcat(). These
	functions were already provided by ixemul.library but were not
	exposed by the public header.

	* include/stdint.h: Add public declarations for popcount32() and
	popcount64(), using uint32_t and uint64_t to match the public
	NetBSD-style interface. The underlying ixemul implementations
	continue to use the ABI-compatible u_int32_t and u_int64_t
	types.

	* library/stat.c, library/__fstat.c: Cap reported st_blksize at
	32 KiB. Some Amiga filesystem handlers return deliberately
	scaled id_BytesPerBlock values through Info(), and multiplying
	these by ixemul's historical filesystem buffer factor could
	otherwise produce excessively large preferred I/O sizes.
	Preserve the raw id_BytesPerBlock value for st_blocks accounting
	and the existing per-file block-size cache.

	* library/vfprintf.c: Added support for the C99 integer length
	modifiers z, j and t. On the ixemul/m68k ABI, z maps to the
	existing long-integer path for size_t, j to the 64-bit
	quad-integer path for intmax_t/uintmax_t, and t to the normal
	integer path for ptrdiff_t. This also enables the corresponding
	%zn, %jn and %tn conversions through the existing %n handling.

2026-09-27  Jörgen Johansson

	* library/buddy-alloc.c: Validate the size passed to b_free()
	against the recorded allocation size. Added allocation headers
	to direct AllocMem() blocks as well as pooled blocks, and always
	use the recorded base address and size when releasing memory.

	* library/memcmp.c: Added a separate assembler path for 68020
	and later processors, derived from the existing 68000/010
	implementation. The 020+ path omits the address-parity checks
	required on 68000/010 because these processors support unaligned
	longword accesses. Retained the short-input fast path, longword
	comparison loop, byte tail and bytewise resolution of differing
	longwords.

	* library/ix_init.c: Check that the global file-table allocation
	succeeded before calculating pointers into the table. If task
	switcher creation fails, free the file table, clear its
	pointers, clean up the allocator and close the supporting
	libraries before returning initialization failure.

2026-09-25  Jörgen Johansson

	* BUGS: Documented the remaining rare SIGWINCH/input.device
	teardown freeze.

	* TODO: Added notes for further investigation of
	__ix_remove_sigwinch(), handler lifetime, process-exit ordering
	and possible teardown hardening.

	* BUGS_SIGWINCH: Added document describing the SIGWINCH issue.

